    "excerpt": "The Alchemy of Endurance -Dr. Athiya Sultana She wept where none could witness her tears, A soul burdened by unspoken fears. Through endless nights, she questioned her fate, Yet wore her silence,...",
    "fullContent": "The Alchemy of Endurance\n                 -Dr. Athiya Sultana\nShe wept where none could witness her tears,\nA soul burdened by unspoken fears.\nThrough endless nights, she questioned her fate,\nYet wore her silence, composed and sedate.\nShe bartered her dreams for the duties she bore,\nGave pieces of herself, yet was asked for more.\nShe poured out her heart, with nothing to spare,\nYet none saw the weight of the burdens she’d bear.\nNo hand reached to hold her, no voice understood,\nYet she kept moving, steadfast and good.\nBeneath all the silence, her purpose stayed bright,\nA coal that kept glowing through the longest night.\nAnd now she stands where her dreams have come true,\nA life once imagined, now lived in full view.\nHer name carries strength; her work speaks with pride,\nShe walks with a freedom she once held inside.\nYet those who endured her despair and defeat\nFind her success a truth hard to meet.\nThey could bear her breaking, but not her becoming;\nHer rise leaves their old expectations crumbling.\nBut she owes no one the dimming of her light,\nNo apology for claiming her height.\nLet envy remain where their praise should have been—\nShe has won her own life, and she will not shrink again."
